TI  - The bad neighbor: Prophage competition in Salmonella during macrophage infection.
AB  - Sargen and Helaine discover a prophage competition element in Salmonella that inhibits the lytic cycle of co-resident prophages by cleaving a subset of cellular tRNAs. During Salmonella pathogenesis in macrophages, a persister subset experiences prophage induction and competition, reducing release of immunogenic cellular components and altering macrophage response to infection.
